    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d501">

                <pb facs="0595" n="585" xml:id="pg585"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.796/11–2244: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the
                        United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-11-22T15:00:00-04:00">November 22,
                            1944—3 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>9820. You will have seen the President’s message of yesterday to the Prime
                        Minister<anchor n="14" xml:id="d501-f1"/> concerning the Aviation
                    Conference. We have been asked to request you urgently to impress upon the Prime
                    Minister and Mr. Eden that the President feels most strongly about this
                    matter.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stettinius</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
